{"id": "section-body-05286", "title": "Principles in the management of ARV drug toxicity", "chapterId": "chapter-six", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "MANAGEMENT OF HIV AND AIDS", "Changing ART in Children Under 15 Years", "Principles in the management of ARV drug toxicity"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-05286", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Principles in the management of ARV drug toxicity", "runs": [{"text": "Principles"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ARV"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "drug"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "toxicity"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1741"}}, {"id": "body-05287", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Severe life-threatening reactions: Immediately discontinue all ARV drugs, manage the medical event (i.e. provide symptomatic and supportive therapy) and reintroduce ARV drugs using a modified regimen (i.e. with an ARV substitution for the offending drug) when the patient is stabilized.", "runs": [{"text": "Severe life-threatening reactions", "bold": true}, {"text": ": ", "bold": true, "italic": true}, {"text": "Immediately discontinue all ARV drugs, manage the medical event (i.e. provide symptomatic and supportive therapy) and reintroduce ARV drugs using a modified regimen (i.e. with an ARV substitution for the offending drug) when the patient is stabilized."}]}, {"id": "body-05289", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Severe reactions: Substitute the offending drug without stopping ART", "runs": [{"text": "Severe", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "reactions", "bold": true}, {"text": ":", "italic": true}, {"text": " ", "italic": true}, {"text": "Substitute"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "offending"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "drug"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "without"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stopping"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ART"}]}, {"id": "body-05290", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Moderate reactions: Consider continuation of ART if it is feasible. If the patient does not improve on symptomatic therapy, consider single-drug substitution", "runs": [{"text": "Moderate reactions", "bold": true}, {"text": ": ", "italic": true}, {"text": "Consider continuation of ART if it is feasible. If the patient does not improve on symptomatic therapy, consider single-drug substitution"}]}, {"id": "body-05292", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Mild reactions: Reassure a child and caregiver that while the reaction may be bothersome, it does not require a change in therapy; provide counselling and support to mitigate adverse reactions.", "runs": [{"text": "Mild reactions", "bold": true}, {"text": ": Reassure a child and caregiver that while the reaction may be bothersome, it does not require a change in therapy; provide counselling and support to mitigate adverse reactions."}]}, {"id": "body-05293", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Emphasize on the maintenance of adherence despite mild and moderate reactions.", "runs": [{"text": "Emphasize"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maintenance"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "adherence"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "despite"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mild"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "moderate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reactions."}]}, {"id": "body-05295", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Table 6.21 Suggested ARV Substitutions", "runs": [{"text": "Table"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "6.21"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Suggested"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ARV"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Substitutions"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-05296", "type": "table", "rows": [{"cells": [{"blocks": [{"id": "body-05296-r1-c1-00002", "typ